.TH LOGSLEUTH 1 "October 2026" "logsleuth 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
logsleuth \- analyze web access logs and sshd auth logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logsleuth
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIfield\fR]
\fIcommand\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B logsleuth
reports on Combined Log Format access logs and sshd authentication logs.
With no \fIFILE\fR it reads standard input.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B summary
Request count, unique client IPs, and a status-class breakdown.
.TP
.B top
The most frequent client IPs, or paths/statuses with \fB\-f\fR.
.TP
.B errors
Counts of 4xx and 5xx responses and the worst paths.
.TP
.B bruteforce
Source IPs in an auth log at or above the failed-login threshold.
Exits 3 if any IP is flagged, so it can gate a pipeline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c \fIfile\fR
Read configuration from \fIfile\fR (keys: top_n, brute_threshold).
.TP
.B \-n \fIN\fR
Limit \fBtop\fR and \fBerrors\fR to \fIN\fR rows.
.TP
.B \-f \fIfield\fR
For \fBtop\fR: \fBip\fR, \fBpath\fR, or \fBstatus\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.B 1
Runtime error (e.g. unreadable file).
.B 2
Usage error.
.B 3
.B bruteforce
flagged at least one IP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
logsleuth summary access.log
logsleuth -n 5 top access.log
cat access.log | logsleuth errors
logsleuth bruteforce /var/log/auth.log
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the Bash Scripting course.
